#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:3
msgid "Content Negotiation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:11
msgid "What is Content Negotiation?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:13
msgid ""
"Content negotiation is a way to determine what type of content to return "
"to the client based on what the client can handle, and what the server "
"can handle. This can be used to determine whether the client is wanting "
"HTML or JSON returned, whether the image should be returned as a JPEG or "
"PNG, what type of compression is supported and more. This is done by "
"analyzing four different headers which can each support multiple value "
"options, each with their own priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:18
msgid ""
"Trying to match this up manually can be pretty challenging. CodeIgniter "
"provides the ``Negotiator`` class that can handle this for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:21
msgid ""
"At it's heart Content Negotiation is simply a part of the HTTP "
"specification that allows a single resource to serve more than one type "
"of content, allowing the clients to request the type of data that works "
"best for them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:25
msgid ""
"A classic example of this is a browser that cannot display PNG files can "
"request only GIF or JPEG images. When the server receives the request, it"
" looks at the available file types the client is requesting and selects "
"the best match from the image formats that it supports, in this case "
"likely choosing a JPEG image to return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:30
msgid "This same negotiation can happen with four types of data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:32
msgid ""
"**Media/Document Type** - this could be image format, or HTML vs. XML or "
"JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:33
msgid ""
"**Character Set** - The character set the returned document should be set"
" in. Typically is UTF-8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:34
msgid ""
"**Document Encoding** - Typically the type of compression used on the "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/content_negotiation.rst:35
msgid ""
"**Document Language** - For sites that support multiple languages, this "
"helps determine which to return."
msgstr ""

